00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.480
So as listeners to Dear Hank and John will already know

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.480
I am a huge fan of the movie Rushmore

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.060
And within that movie there is a play set during the Vietnam War

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.620
in which a character is asked "How long you been in country?"

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.940
And the soldier replies,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.140
"I ain't even here, Sergeant. I'm in Cheyenne, Wyoming."

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.920
Anyway, Cheyenne, Wyoming has since become my personal shorthand

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.260
for the place I visit when I am deeply immersed in a project.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.740
Like, when we first started making Vlogbrothers back in 2007

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.060
I spent several months in Cheyenne because I wasn't really where ever I physically was

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.700
I was always thinking about what my next video was gonna be about

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.040
or how to grow our audience or about how cool YouTube was

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.600
But mostly I visit Cheyenne, Wyoming when I'm writing

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.820
Now, in a lot of ways being in Cheyenne is super fun

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.500
Like one of my primary complaints about human life is that we spend

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.940
the entire enterprise stuck inside of one particular slowly decaying body

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.620
and living inside of a made up world has always allowed me to feel free from that

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.060
Like free from the twin prisons from my consciousness and my body

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.820
But also for much of my life Cheyenne has been kind of an escape

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:02.080
like all those years when I didn't have many real friends and I felt intensely lonely

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.620
I could always go to Cheyenne where people would like me because, you know, I'd made the up.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.520
That said when I'm in Cheyenne I'm also kind of, you know, like

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.860
not here, which means that sometimes I'll be at dinner with my kids and not answer when I'm asked a question

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.080
I neglect daily responsibilities, I forget to get haircuts.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.540
I've been in Cheyenne, Wyoming for quite a while now and I expect to be here a while longer

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.840
And It can be really frustrating because I actually like my real life

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:31.440
And I like making videos every tuesday 
and I'm not all the way here and I worry I should be

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:36.440
because the other thing about going to Cheyenne is that you aren't necessarily going to come home with anything

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.140
Like I spent about a year in Cheyenne finishing the Fault in our Stars

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.620
but I also spent several months there a few years ago only to realize that the book I'd worked so hard on

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.740
Wasn't very good  and wasn't gonna be published

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.240
For me at least I can't know until after I immerse myself in the work

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.980
Which is frustrating and scary but

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.300
You know what, actually, no "but" it's just frustrating and scary at the moment

