Hank, in your video last week you talked about how to be productive

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.680
And I thought you gave very helpful and astute advice

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.540
But I think creative productivity is somewhat different

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:09.600
because for one thing you have to spend time in ways that markets and our culture don't really recognize as productive

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:12.920
Like reading or pacing or staring out the window

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.020
and then once you get deep enough into the work you have to make space in your life

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.360
and ask the people around you to to make space in their lives for you to go to Cheyenne, Wyoming

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.800
Now that doesn't mean working all day every day. I wrote my first two books at night after work

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.040
and wrote them quicker than I have any book since

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.420
but it does mean that a certain percentage of your intellectual and  emotional self will be absent for a while

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.580
then you make what you can of your time in Cheyenne, then, most importantly, you come home

